  "implementation": [
    "One-shot existing owner-authenticated LAN GET: fixed port/path, private address and token checks, manual redirects/no credential reuse or cookies/cache, aggregate2048-byte body cap, nonrenewable10-second deadline and late/backwards-clock refusal. No retries or mutation verbs.",
    "Trusted immutable upgrade catalogue bound to exact backend model, firmware, profile, predecessor BLAKE2b digest and publisher key. Duplicate transitions refuse the catalogue. Independently pinned downloaded package identities must match the chosen transition.",
    "Ordinary Prepare update action loads the existing owner credential solely for read-only inventory; a known transition proceeds to HTTPS download and exact-plan review. Local development preparation remains separate and explicitly unqualified.",
    "Exact-plan approval reloads the owner credential and compares its fingerprint, then rechecks the installed release before starting the existing coordinator. Changed predecessor/owner/session/hardware identity, unavailable read, cancellation and stale callbacks refuse before installation starts."
  ],
